# AI-Driven Construction PM Simulator — Detailed Spec (35 lines)

1) Goal: interactive web app where users define WBS/resources/budget/risk, run CPM-based simulations, and see live KPIs (SV, CV) + AI insights; scope = single project per user in MVP, multi-project later.
2) Users & Roles: Student (create/iterate simulations), Instructor (create locked scenarios, view class comparisons), Admin (manage catalog, feature flags); auth via Firebase Email+Google OAuth.
3) UX Principles: uncluttered dashboard; guided 3-step flow (Setup → Simulate → Analyze); real-time updates (optimistic UI + server confirmations); responsive (≥1280 desktop target, mobile read-only MVP).
4) Tech Stack Frontend: React 18 + Vite; MUI components; React Router; Redux Toolkit (project, wbs, sim slices); Recharts (KPIs); DHTMLX Gantt (timeline); .env via Vite; ESLint/Prettier.
5) Tech Stack Backend: FastAPI (Python 3.11), Uvicorn; SQLAlchemy + Alembic; PostgreSQL 15; Pydantic v2 schemas; Celery/RQ worker for long simulations; Redis for job queue + cache.
6) Hosting/CI: Frontend on Vercel (preview PRs, env vars); Backend+DB on Render/Heroku (Procfile, health check, autosleep off); CI GitHub Actions (lint/test/build; db migrations on main).
7) Data Model: Projects(id, owner_id, name, scope, budget, start,end, created_at); Tasks(id, project_id, parent_id, name, duration_days, cost, predecessors[], resource_demand json); Resources(id, project_id, name, type, unit_cost, capacity); Risks(id, project_id, description, probability, impact_days, impact_cost); SimRuns(id, project_id, status, seed, created_at); SimLogs(id, sim_id, ts, event, delta_days, delta_cost).
8) Indexes: tasks(project_id), tasks(predecessors GIN), simlogs(sim_id, ts), risks(project_id); FK cascades on project delete; DB constraints on dates (end ≥ start).
9) API Contracts (JSON): POST /auth/login (Firebase token verify); GET/POST /projects; GET/PUT /projects/:id; GET/POST /projects/:id/tasks; GET/POST /projects/:id/resources; GET/POST /projects/:id/risks; POST /simulate (project_id, seed?); GET /simulate/:sim_id/status; GET /simulate/:sim_id/results; GET /kpi/:project_id/current.
10) Validation: Pydantic models enforce positive duration/cost; cycle detection in predecessors; resource capacity ≥ 0; budget ≥ Σ task cost; risk probability ∈ [0,1].
11) CPM Algorithm: build DAG from tasks; topological sort; compute ES/EF, then LS/LF; critical path = tasks with zero float; baseline schedule persisted per project version.
12) Resource Leveling (heuristic MVP): greedy shift non-critical tasks within float by earliest resource availability; minimize peak overload; recompute KPIs post-leveling.
13) Simulation Engine: deterministic baseline (CPM) + risk injection; each tick applies events from Risks (Bernoulli draw by probability); when triggered, adjust task duration/cost per impact; log events; recompute path and SV/CV.
14) KPIs: SV = EV−PV (days or cost proxy); CV = EV−AC; REI = Σ(probability×impact normalized); trend lines via Recharts; status LEDs (Green/Amber/Red) by thresholds.
15) Gantt Updates: WebSocket/SSE from FastAPI for sim progress; frontend listens and updates DHTMLX Gantt + KPI cards; fall back to polling /simulate/:id/status every 2s.
16) State Slices: projectSlice (meta, dates, budget), wbsSlice (tasks, edges), resourceSlice, riskSlice, simulationSlice (status, simId, logs), kpiSlice (sv, cv, rei, trends).
17) Forms & Guards: ProjectSetup form (Zod/Yup client validation + server checks); route guards require Firebase ID token; instructor routes check custom claim.
18) AI Integration (Post-MVP): POST /ai/insights {project_snapshot} → Gemini 1.5 (system prompt defines role: PM advisor; constraints: actionable, cite risks/tasks); responses cached 10 min (hash of snapshot).
19) Prompt Content: summary of critical path, top-3 risks (prob×impact), slack distribution, overload hotspots, budget variance; request prioritized mitigations with cost/benefit.
20) Accessibility: MUI defaults; semantic headings; keyboard nav; ARIA labels on KPI cards/Gantt; color-contrast ≥ 4.5:1; prefers-reduced-motion honored on chart animations.
21) Error Handling: typed errors (400 validation, 404 not found, 409 concurrency, 500 sim failure); toast messages + retry; backend logs with correlation_id per request.
22) Security: Firebase token verification middleware; row-level auth (owner or instructor); rate limit /ai/* and /simulate/*; input sanitization; CORS restricted to frontend origin.
23) Performance: paginate tasks (server-side); compress JSON (gzip); cache GET /kpi; defer heavy calculations to worker; lazy-load Gantt route; code-split per page.
24) Testing Backend: pytest (unit: CPM, leveling, risk); fastapi TestClient for endpoints; factory data; 90% coverage on algorithms; seed reproducibility tests.
25) Testing Frontend: Vitest + React Testing Library; snapshot KPI cards; router tests; WebSocket mock for sim stream; E2E Playwright: setup→simulate→analyze path.
26) Seed Data: fixture project “Campus Build” with 25 tasks, 3 resources, 5 risks; ensures demo-ready preview; include CSV import for tasks/resources in MVP+1.
27) Logging & Observability: structured JSON logs (uvicorn); request timing; Celery task durations; Grafana (optional) or simple /health and /metrics endpoints.
28) i18n & Locale: en-NO defaults; number/date format via Intl; text keys externalized for later localization (nb, en).
29) Deploy Pipeline: PR → lint/test → preview (Vercel) + staging API; on main merge → migrate DB (Alembic) → deploy backend → smoke test /health → promote.
30) Config Flags: feature_gantt_panning, feature_ai_insights, feature_multi_user; instructor can pin scenario (lock edits) via admin UI (post-MVP).
31) Data Export: /reports/:project_id (CSV: tasks/resources/risks; JSON: sim logs; PDF summary post-MVP using WeasyPrint).
32) Backup/Restore: nightly PG dump; retention 7 days in MVP; restore script documented; anonymize PII in dumps.
33) Timeline (6 weeks): W1 setup/auth; W2 DB+CRUD; W3 Gantt read-only; W4 CPM+simulation worker; W5 KPIs + real-time + polish; W6 tests, hardening, deploy.
34) Success Criteria: create→simulate→analyze flow works; KPIs accurate vs textbook cases; Gantt updates in near-real-time; AI insights actionable and consistent.
35) Risks & Mitigations: Gantt complexity→PoC early; algorithm correctness→unit tests + reference cases; scope creep→strict MVP; hosting limits→staging perf tests.
